Build fix, macOS: features switched off that upstream always builds.

The Mac port is built upstream with every feature on. profiles/macos turns
some off (encrypted media, web extensions), and that shows what was only
held together by the rest being there:

- WebDriver's protocol has the commands that load and unload a web
  extension whether or not extensions are built, and the class that
  implements the protocol declared them only when they are, which left it
  abstract. They are now always there, and answer "not implemented"
  without extensions.
- Sources are compiled several to a file, and three of them used what a
  neighbour had included or switched off for them: a conversion from
  NSData, WKErrorDomain, and the permission to call a method that macOS 27
  deprecates. With the neighbour compiling to nothing they have to say so
  themselves.
- A parameter that is used only for encrypted media.

